194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054404 1074 "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number\n$(-3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} (2y+7) \\cdot (-3) \\\\[5pt] &= 2y\\cdot(-3)+7\\cdot(-3) \\\\[5pt] &= (-6y) + (-21) \\\\[5pt] &= -6y-21 \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 false] [17592186054404 1074 "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number \n$(-3)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t(2y+7) \\cdot (-3)&=\\[5pt]\n\t2y\\cdot(-3)+7\\cdot(-3)&=\\[5pt]\n\t(-6y) + (-21)&=\\[5pt]\n\t-6y-21\n\t}\n$$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054405 1071 "Expand $7(5x-3y)$." 13194139534941 17592186045417 false] [17592186054405 1071 "Expand $7(5x-3y).$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054405 1074 "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $7\\mathbin$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7(5x - 3y) &=  \\\\\n7 \\cdot 5x + 7 \\cdot (-3y) &=  \\\\\n(35x) + (-21y) &=  \\\\\n&= 35x - 21y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 false] [17592186054405 1074 "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $7\\mathbin:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(5x-3y) & = \\\\ 7\\cdot 5x+7\\cdot (-3y) & = \\\\ (35x)+(-21y) & = \\\\ 35x-21y & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054406 1071 "Expand $-11(4x - 3y) .$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054406 1071 "Expand $-11(4x - 3y)$." 13194139534941 17592186045417 false] [17592186054406 1074 "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $(-11)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-11(4x - 3y) &=  \\\\\n(-11) \\cdot 4x + (-11) \\cdot (-3y) &=  \\\\\n(-44x) + (33y) &=  \\\\\n&= - 44x + 33y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 false] [17592186054406 1074 "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $(-11)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-11(4x-3y) & = \\\\ (-11)\\cdot 4x+(-11)\\cdot (-3y) & = \\\\ (-44x)+(33y) & = \\\\ -44x+33y & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054777 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445155 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054778 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445153 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054778 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445154 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054779 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445151 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054779 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445152 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054780 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445149 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054780 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445150 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186054885 1050 420.0 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186055379 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186055379 1071 "$5(8x+3)=$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186055379 1071 "What is $5(8x + 3)$?" 13194139534941 17592186045417 false] [17592186055379 1074 "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(8x+3) & = \\\\ 5\\cdot 8x+5\\cdot 3 & = \\\\ 40x+15\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186056023 1064 "The **distributive law** states that multiplying a group of terms by a number is the same as multiplying each term separately by that same number and adding the products.\n\nFor example, let's take a look at the following expression:\n\n$$\n2(3+4)\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this expression using the distributive law:\n\n![](images/4c/4ca32844e45f756ce88e4d8e6d73e8b69099d2c517157b51fed9bb1f02a699ea.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(3 + 4) &=  \\\\\n2 \\cdot 3 + 2 \\cdot 4 &=  \\\\\n6 + 8 &=  \\\\\n&= 14 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe distributive law also applies when the multiplication occurs on the right of the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(3 + 4) \\cdot 2 &=  \\\\\n3 \\cdot 2 + 4 \\cdot 2 &=  \\\\\n6 + 8 &=  \\\\\n&= 14\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 false] [17592186056023 1064 "The **distributive law** states that multiplying a group of terms by a number is the same as multiplying each term separately by that same number and adding the products.\n\nFor example, let's take a look at the following expression: \n\n$$\n2(3+4).\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can evaluate this expression using the distributive law:\n\n![](images/4c/4ca32844e45f756ce88e4d8e6d73e8b69099d2c517157b51fed9bb1f02a699ea.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3+4) & = \\\\ 2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ 6+8 & = \\\\ 14 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe distributive law also applies when the multiplication occurs on the right of the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+4)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ 3\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ 6+8 & = \\\\ 14 & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186056024 1064 "The distributive law also works when there is subtraction inside the parentheses.\n\nFor example, we can expand the expression $2(3-4)$ as follows:\n\n![](images/05/05ba4424f566b35af2a279b994c3a8f13564560deaa60f1c7c4616f52d2fb8d6.png)\n\nNotice that we keep a plus ($+$) sign between the two terms. This helps us to avoid mistakes when multiplying with negative numbers.\n\nNow, evaluating our expression, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(3 - 4) &=  \\\\\n2 \\cdot 3 + 2 \\cdot (-4) &=  \\\\\n(6) + (-8) &=  \\\\\n6 - 8 &=  \\\\\n&= - 2 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distributive law also applies when the multiplication occurs on the right of the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(3 - 4) \\cdot 2 &=  \\\\\n3 \\cdot 2 + (-4) \\cdot 2 &=  \\\\\n(6) + (-8) &=  \\\\\n6 - 8 &=  \\\\\n&= - 2 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 false] [17592186056024 1064 "The distributive law also works when there is subtraction inside the parentheses. \n\nFor example, we can expand the expression $2(3-4)$ as follows:\n\n![](images/05/05ba4424f566b35af2a279b994c3a8f13564560deaa60f1c7c4616f52d2fb8d6.png)\n\nNotice that we keep a plus ($+$) sign between the two terms. This helps us to avoid mistakes when multiplying with negative numbers.\n\nNow, evaluating our expression, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3-4) & = \\\\ 2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot (-4) & = \\\\ (6)+(-8) & = \\\\ 6-8 & = \\\\ -2 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distributive law also applies when the multiplication occurs on the right of the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-4)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ 3\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ (6)+(-8) & = \\\\ 6-8 & = \\\\ -2 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445112 1080 "-40" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445112 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445112 1083 #uuid "071411a0-3d13-5b6d-acf3-f829e6765509" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445113 1080 "40x-15" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445113 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445113 1083 #uuid "17a71d18-2373-5b34-b0ee-6cee8fb4daac" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445114 1080 "15" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445114 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445114 1083 #uuid "1eea5216-9dec-522d-8e89-e2a2e3d59f9e" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445115 1080 "-40x+15" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445115 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445115 1083 #uuid "340a5ab9-11ca-55a1-86ac-9be79f5a7430" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445116 1080 "40x+15" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445116 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445116 1083 #uuid "356915f5-cbce-57bf-8584-53e5840fc46d" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445117 1080 "-7k+14i" 13194139534941 17592186045417 true] [17592186445117 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139